1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,795
A sticky, yellowish film on your kitchen
cabinets,

2
00:00:03,970 --> 00:00:06,976
worst above the stove and around the
handles?

3
00:00:07,267 --> 00:00:08,346
Don't scrub.

4
00:00:09,310 --> 00:00:12,783
Seven steps dissolve it with gentle
products, with

5
00:00:12,793 --> 00:00:14,464
no damage to the finish.

6
00:00:15,615 --> 00:00:18,786
Stay for step four: the waiting does the

7
00:00:18,796 --> 00:00:19,979
work for you.

8
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:21,574
WikiTube.

9
00:00:21,865 --> 00:00:24,093
Whatever it is, here's how.

10
00:00:24,367 --> 00:00:28,153
Cabinet grease is cooking oil vapor, steam
and

11
00:00:28,163 --> 00:00:30,960
dust, stuck to every surface.

12
00:00:31,321 --> 00:00:33,808
The trick is a degreaser that breaks the

13
00:00:33,818 --> 00:00:38,008
oil down, not hard scrubbing, which wears
the finish.

14
00:00:38,671 --> 00:00:41,169
We start with the mildest option and move

15
00:00:41,179 --> 00:00:42,664
up only if needed.

16
00:00:43,210 --> 00:00:46,391
Always test a cleaner in a hidden spot
first.

17
00:00:46,933 --> 00:00:49,756
You'll need warm water and dish soap,
baking

18
00:00:49,766 --> 00:00:53,959
soda, soft microfiber cloths, an old soft

19
00:00:53,969 --> 00:00:58,173
toothbrush, and white vinegar, only for
sealed or painted

20
00:00:58,183 --> 00:00:59,053
cabinets.

21
00:00:59,507 --> 00:01:02,548
No steel wool, no oven cleaner.

22
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:04,121
Step one.

23
00:01:04,412 --> 00:01:06,817
Clear the counter below the cabinets and
lay

24
00:01:06,827 --> 00:01:08,835
down a towel to catch drips.

25
00:01:09,126 --> 00:01:11,833
Find out what the cabinet finish is:
sealed

26
00:01:11,843 --> 00:01:15,964
wood, painted wood, laminate or
thermofoil.

27
00:01:16,510 --> 00:01:18,648
Then test your cleaning mix on a hidden

28
00:01:18,658 --> 00:01:21,072
spot, such as the inside of a door

29
00:01:21,131 --> 00:01:24,253
or the bottom edge, and wait a few
minutes.

30
00:01:24,614 --> 00:01:28,629
If there's no discoloration or softening,
you're good to go.

31
00:01:28,921 --> 00:01:32,370
Raw or unfinished wood needs much less
moisture

32
00:01:32,380 --> 00:01:33,900
than other finishes.

33
00:01:34,354 --> 00:01:36,596
If you're unsure about the finish, ask the

34
00:01:36,606 --> 00:01:40,089
manufacturer or use only mild soap and
water.

35
00:01:40,751 --> 00:01:43,188
Gloves help keep your hands soft.

36
00:01:43,733 --> 00:01:44,928
Step two.

37
00:01:45,591 --> 00:01:48,239
Before you add any liquid, wipe the
cabinets

38
00:01:48,249 --> 00:01:51,188
with a dry microfiber cloth to remove
loose

39
00:01:51,198 --> 00:01:53,264
dust, lint and crumbs.

40
00:01:53,926 --> 00:01:56,703
Grease and dust together form a sticky
paste,

41
00:01:56,713 --> 00:01:59,083
which becomes harder to clean once it's
wet

42
00:01:59,093 --> 00:02:00,392
and smeared around.

43
00:02:01,194 --> 00:02:03,750
Work from the top down, and pay attention

44
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:06,511
to the tops of cabinet doors, the corners

45
00:02:06,639 --> 00:02:08,739
and the area around the handles.

46
00:02:09,890 --> 00:02:12,492
A vacuum with a brush attachment is
helpful

47
00:02:12,502 --> 00:02:14,568
for carved or ridged doors.

48
00:02:14,801 --> 00:02:17,670
Don't skip this, since wiping a dusty
surface

49
00:02:17,680 --> 00:02:19,876
with a wet cloth turns the dirt into

50
00:02:19,886 --> 00:02:20,988
a grey smear.

51
00:02:21,533 --> 00:02:22,519
Step three.

52
00:02:22,973 --> 00:02:25,491
Fill a bowl or bucket with warm water,

53
00:02:25,724 --> 00:02:28,672
and add a few drops of grease-cutting dish
soap.

54
00:02:29,822 --> 00:02:32,584
Stir it gently until it's slightly sudsy.

55
00:02:33,131 --> 00:02:36,857
This simple mix dissolves cooking oil on
most finishes.

56
00:02:37,311 --> 00:02:40,189
For sealed or painted cabinets with heavy
buildup,

57
00:02:40,213 --> 00:02:42,014
you can use a half and half mix

58
00:02:42,024 --> 00:02:44,879
of white vinegar and warm water instead.

59
00:02:45,844 --> 00:02:50,243
Avoid vinegar on unfinished wood, natural
stone countertops

60
00:02:50,418 --> 00:02:52,042
and any glue seams.

61
00:02:53,007 --> 00:02:57,197
Never combine different cleaning products,
and never use bleach.

62
00:02:58,347 --> 00:03:01,493
Prepare a fresh batch if the water turns
cloudy.

63
00:03:02,643 --> 00:03:05,466
Warm water works much better than cold
water

64
00:03:05,476 --> 00:03:06,775
on cooking oil.

65
00:03:07,333 --> 00:03:08,307
Step four.

66
00:03:08,970 --> 00:03:11,943
Dip a microfiber cloth in the solution and

67
00:03:11,953 --> 00:03:15,529
wring it out well, so it's damp but not
dripping.

68
00:03:16,679 --> 00:03:19,084
Wipe a small section of the cabinet, and

69
00:03:19,094 --> 00:03:21,914
then let the solution sit for a minute or
two.

70
00:03:22,577 --> 00:03:25,168
This dwell time lets the soap soften the

71
00:03:25,178 --> 00:03:27,661
grease, so you don't need to scrub.

72
00:03:28,811 --> 00:03:32,050
Rinse the cloth often, as it picks up oil.

73
00:03:32,596 --> 00:03:36,174
Work in small sections, using gentle
circles, and

74
00:03:36,184 --> 00:03:38,900
move from the top of the cabinet to the
bottom.

75
00:03:39,446 --> 00:03:41,816
Use a second cloth to rinse and wring

76
00:03:41,826 --> 00:03:43,265
it out regularly.

77
00:03:44,415 --> 00:03:46,669
It is better to take more passes than

78
00:03:46,679 --> 00:03:48,304
to use more liquid.

79
00:03:48,867 --> 00:03:50,015
Step five.

80
00:03:50,980 --> 00:03:54,487
For stubborn, thick grease, mix baking
soda with

81
00:03:54,497 --> 00:03:57,051
a little water to make a soft paste.

82
00:03:57,412 --> 00:03:59,666
Spread it on the sticky areas, let it

83
00:03:59,676 --> 00:04:02,220
sit for five minutes, and gently work it

84
00:04:02,230 --> 00:04:05,422
with the soft toothbrush, in small
circles.

85
00:04:06,224 --> 00:04:09,488
Baking soda is mildly abrasive, so use
light

86
00:04:09,498 --> 00:04:13,990
pressure, and avoid it on high-gloss
finishes, which can dull.

87
00:04:14,955 --> 00:04:18,021
Pay attention to the handles, hinges and
the

88
00:04:18,031 --> 00:04:19,830
grooves of paneled doors.

89
00:04:20,191 --> 00:04:23,150
Wipe the paste away with a clean damp
cloth.

90
00:04:23,511 --> 00:04:26,171
Go slowly near hinges and edges, where the

91
00:04:26,181 --> 00:04:27,655
finish is thinnest.

92
00:04:28,016 --> 00:04:31,370
A pea-sized amount of paste goes a long
way.

93
00:04:31,933 --> 00:04:33,012
Step six.

94
00:04:33,373 --> 00:04:36,251
Go over every surface with a second cloth,

95
00:04:36,426 --> 00:04:40,457
dampened with plain water, to remove soap
and

96
00:04:40,467 --> 00:04:42,068
any leftover grease.

97
00:04:43,218 --> 00:04:45,911
Soap residue can attract new dirt.

98
00:04:46,574 --> 00:04:50,648
Then immediately dry the cabinets with a
dry microfiber cloth.

99
00:04:51,798 --> 00:04:54,401
Moisture left on wood can cause swelling
or

100
00:04:54,411 --> 00:04:57,637
stains, especially near the edges and
joints.

101
00:04:58,787 --> 00:05:01,643
Check the cabinets in the light from a few
angles.

102
00:05:02,793 --> 00:05:05,453
If you see sticky patches, repeat the
previous

103
00:05:05,463 --> 00:05:07,552
step on just those spots.

104
00:05:07,913 --> 00:05:10,074
A quick pass with a clean dry cloth

105
00:05:10,084 --> 00:05:13,661
also removes streaks, and leaves the
surface smooth

106
00:05:13,671 --> 00:05:14,576
to the touch.

107
00:05:15,133 --> 00:05:16,235
Step seven.

108
00:05:17,200 --> 00:05:20,554
Prevention takes far less effort than
cleaning.

109
00:05:21,101 --> 00:05:24,225
Use your extractor fan or range hood
whenever

110
00:05:24,235 --> 00:05:27,659
you cook, and clean its filters monthly.

111
00:05:28,321 --> 00:05:30,866
Wipe the cabinets above the stove and
around

112
00:05:30,876 --> 00:05:33,499
handles every week with a damp cloth.

113
00:05:34,649 --> 00:05:37,864
Cover pans while frying to cut down on
spatter.

114
00:05:38,410 --> 00:05:40,641
If your cabinets have a new buildup layer,

115
00:05:40,651 --> 00:05:42,497
you'll remove it much faster.

116
00:05:43,043 --> 00:05:45,599
Keep a cloth near the stove, and wipe

117
00:05:45,609 --> 00:05:47,617
splashes on the day they happen.

118
00:05:48,419 --> 00:05:50,603
Wash the filters of your range hood in

119
00:05:50,613 --> 00:05:53,668
hot soapy water once a month, since
clogged

120
00:05:53,678 --> 00:05:56,057
filters push grease into the room.

121
00:05:56,600 --> 00:05:59,353
If a spot still feels tacky, the grease

122
00:05:59,363 --> 00:06:00,779
has probably hardened.

123
00:06:01,442 --> 00:06:03,637
Lay a cloth wrung out in hot soapy

124
00:06:03,647 --> 00:06:05,507
water on the spot for a couple of

125
00:06:05,517 --> 00:06:08,081
minutes to soften it, then wipe.

126
00:06:08,883 --> 00:06:12,066
Handles and knobs get the oiliest, so
clean

127
00:06:12,076 --> 00:06:13,886
them with a soft toothbrush.

128
00:06:14,340 --> 00:06:17,151
A stickiness that stays after rinsing may
be

129
00:06:17,161 --> 00:06:21,317
leftover soap, so wipe once more with
plain water.

130
00:06:21,867 --> 00:06:25,396
Sometimes the problem is the finish, not
the grease.

131
00:06:26,059 --> 00:06:29,636
Dull patches, peeling edges or swollen
corners mean

132
00:06:29,646 --> 00:06:33,732
the surface is already damaged, and
cleaning cannot fix that.

133
00:06:34,278 --> 00:06:37,876
Thermofoil doors near an oven can peel
because of heat.

134
00:06:38,841 --> 00:06:41,768
For small chips on painted doors, matching
touch-up

135
00:06:41,778 --> 00:06:42,857
paint can help.

136
00:06:43,404 --> 00:06:46,168
If many doors are damaged, a cabinet
painter

137
00:06:46,178 --> 00:06:48,627
or refacing company can advise you.

138
00:06:49,167 --> 00:06:52,045
Some habits keep grease away from the
doors.

139
00:06:52,406 --> 00:06:55,423
Use a splatter screen on the pan when you
fry.

140
00:06:55,877 --> 00:06:58,096
Wipe the oil bottle and spice jars you

141
00:06:58,106 --> 00:07:00,813
keep near the stove, because they carry
grease

142
00:07:00,823 --> 00:07:02,865
onto the cabinets when you touch them.

143
00:07:03,667 --> 00:07:05,317
Let the range hood run for a few

144
00:07:05,327 --> 00:07:08,856
minutes after cooking, to clear the
airborne grease.

145
00:07:09,217 --> 00:07:12,211
Dust the tops of the cabinets once a
season.

146
00:07:12,767 --> 00:07:14,600
Here are the mistakes to avoid.

147
00:07:14,961 --> 00:07:17,619
First, using too much water on wood.

148
00:07:17,980 --> 00:07:21,136
It can swell, warp or stain the surface,

149
00:07:21,160 --> 00:07:23,969
so keep the cloth damp, not wet.

150
00:07:25,119 --> 00:07:28,871
Second, scrubbing hard with abrasive pads,
which scratch

151
00:07:28,881 --> 00:07:31,887
the finish and make future grease stick
even more.

152
00:07:32,550 --> 00:07:35,997
And third, using harsh chemicals without
testing.

153
00:07:36,799 --> 00:07:39,294
Some cleaners strip paint or varnish.

154
00:07:39,748 --> 00:07:43,149
Be gentle, test first, and let the soap

155
00:07:43,173 --> 00:07:44,089
do the work.

156
00:07:44,891 --> 00:07:48,164
A little patience beats a lot of scrubbing
every time.

157
00:07:48,700 --> 00:07:49,848
Let's recap.

158
00:07:50,511 --> 00:07:53,494
Clear the area and test in a hidden spot.

159
00:07:54,644 --> 00:07:56,524
Dust and dry wipe first.

160
00:07:57,326 --> 00:07:59,032
Mix a gentle degreaser.

161
00:08:00,182 --> 00:08:01,609
Wipe and let it work.

162
00:08:02,156 --> 00:08:04,523
Treat thick buildup with baking soda.

163
00:08:05,325 --> 00:08:07,159
Rinse and dry thoroughly.

164
00:08:07,612 --> 00:08:09,669
And stop the grease from coming back with

165
00:08:09,679 --> 00:08:10,839
a weekly wipe.

166
00:08:11,989 --> 00:08:15,811
Seven steps, about an hour, and kitchen
cabinets

167
00:08:15,821 --> 00:08:17,306
that feel clean again.

168
00:08:17,969 --> 00:08:21,080
If it stays sticky, soften it with warmth,

169
00:08:21,371 --> 00:08:23,727
and keep grease away with a few habits.

170
00:08:24,267 --> 00:08:27,761
That's how you remove sticky grease from
kitchen cabinets.

171
00:08:28,308 --> 00:08:31,918
If your cabinets look brighter, subscribe
to WikiTube,

172
00:08:32,046 --> 00:08:35,621
because we publish a new how-to every
single day.

173
00:08:35,982 --> 00:08:38,108
Tell us in the comments which cabinet was

174
00:08:38,118 --> 00:08:40,442
the stickiest, and what you would like us

175
00:08:40,452 --> 00:08:41,856
to explain next.

176
00:08:42,216 --> 00:08:43,284
See you tomorrow.

177
00:08:43,645 --> 00:08:45,492
Don't forget to give the handles a wipe

178
00:08:45,502 --> 00:08:46,755
before you go.

179
00:08:46,867 --> 00:08:48,132
That's WikiTube.

180
00:08:48,365 --> 00:08:50,733
Whatever it is, here's how.
